\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the first $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\cdot {C}_{31}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+5\\cdot {C}_{33} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}+5\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}+5\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1-4)+5(6-3) \\\\  & =-3+15 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the second $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix} & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+2\\cdot {C}_{22}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(5+4)+(0-2) \\\\  & =18-2 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}=1\\cdot 12-2\\cdot 16=-20.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
